Project: {{config.metadata.name}} ({{stack}} / {{architecture}})
Doc language: {{language}}

Help register a BPMS / workflow engine integration (Camunda 7/8/Zeebe, Flowable, Temporal, Conductor).
Return ONLY a JSON object — no Markdown fences, no prose.

User input:
"""
{{extra.userDescription}}
"""

Schema:
{
  "name": string,                        // e.g. "Camunda 8"
  "vendor": string,                      // optional
  "purpose": string,
  "endpoints": [{ "name": string, "protocol": string, "url": string }],
  "slaTargets": { "availability": string, "latencyP95Ms": number },   // optional
  "auth": { "mode": string, "secretsRef": string },                   // optional
  "errorHandling": string,                                            // optional
  "rateLimits": string,                                               // optional
  "observability": string,                                            // optional
  "versioning": string,                                               // optional
  "extra": {
    "engine": string,                    // "camunda-8" | "camunda-7" | "temporal" | "flowable" | ...
    "processes": string[],
    "jobWorkers": string[],
    "correlationKeys": string[],
    "sagas": string[],
    "retentionDays": number,
    "versioning": string,
    "bpmnFile": string                   // optional path to .bpmn for diagram import
  }
}

Constraints:
- Do NOT include "id" — INT-NNN is assigned by the tool.
- Cover process retention, retries, correlation, saga compensation, deployment versioning.

Return JSON only.
